&#8220;A couple Christmases ago Dolly gifted me this vinyl knowing how much I’d love an original,&#8221; the singer-actress wrote. &#8220;My Aunt Dolly is one of the greatest songwriters the world has ever known. She never made music for recognition but to make the world a happier place through her songs.&#8221;

Cyrus also shared a clip of her in the studio recording vocals for the 2026 version of &#8220;Light of a Clear Blue Morning,&#8221; which Parton and her collaborators released in January in honor of the icon&#8217;s 80th birthday. She&#8217;d pass away about eight months later following a brief cancer battle .

&#8220;To be nominated alongside her, Lainey Wilson, Queen Latifah and Reba McEntire for Light of a Clear Blue Morning is a beautiful way to honor her enormous heart,&#8221; Cyrus continued in her post. &#8220;This cover supported pediatric cancer research at Vanderbilt’s Monroe Carell Jr. Children’s Hospital a cause close to her heart.&#8221;

The Hannah Montana alum added: &#8220;I miss her calling on big days like this but feel her in every moment. Love you Aunt Dolly. Congratulations to these beautiful women and all the other nominees.&#8221;

Parton is actually nominated twice in the best country duo/group performance category, earning a nod for her guest appearance on Zac Brown Band&#8217;s &#8220;Butterfly.&#8221; Her narration of her book Star of the Show: My Life on Stage also got a spot in the best Audio Book, narration and storytelling recording race.

The Dollywood founder won a total of 10 Grammys in her lifetime out of 58 nominations. &#8220;Light of a Clear Blue Morning&#8221; &#8212; which debuted at No. 1 on the Billboard Country Digital Song Sales chart &#8212; was just one of several songs on which Parton collaborated with Cyrus. The pair also collaborated on a joint version of Cyrus&#8217; hit &#8220;Wrecking Ball&#8221; as well as &#8220;Rainbowland&#8221; from Cyrus&#8217; album Younger Now.

The 2027 Grammys will take place on Feb. 7. RAYE leads the upcoming ceremony&#8217;s nominations with 11 total, followed by Rosalia with nine.
